text:
Score: 5/10.

I would not approve this as-is. The tiny demo and integration test are broken from a clean checkout because the required story dataset is missing, and the default/full HF path has multiple untested correctness risks. The core tiny-mode math is reasonably compact, but the repo is not currently reproducible enough for active development.

Verification: copied repo to `/tmp`, installed `.[test]`, ran `pytest`: 6 passed, 1 failed (`test_tiny_end_to_end`) due missing `data/stories/manifest.json`. Running tests directly in `/work` also failed before collection because dependencies were not installed in the base environment.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change scope: about 220 LOC.

```json
{
  "score": 5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "emovec/data.py",
      "lines": "24-36",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Extraction unconditionally requires data/stories/manifest.json and story files, but the repo does not include or generate them, so the documented demo and integration test fail."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/test_integration_tiny.py",
      "lines": "12-24",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "The end-to-end tiny test depends on missing fixture data, making the clean-checkout test suite red."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/validate_contexts.py",
      "lines": "21-29",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Validation loads vectors and instantiates the requested backend without checking manifest backend, layer count, or d_model compatibility."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/steer_prefs.py",
      "lines": "25-30",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Preference steering also trusts vector artifacts without validating that they match the backend/model being evaluated."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "226-241",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "HF steering falls back to all prompt tokens when offsets are unavailable, so non-fast tokenizers steer the whole prompt instead of only the activity span."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "306-308",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Preference scoring assumes ' good' and ' bad' are valid single-token labels and silently uses only the first token for multi-token encodings."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "243-250",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "HF activation extraction has no max_length/truncation handling, so long stories can exceed the model context window and crash."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "204-214",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The HF backend's dtype='auto' path loads the model at default precision and then moves it to device, increasing the chance of avoidable OOMs."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/config.py",
      "lines": "42-72",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Config values are not validated, so empty emotions, zero topics, negative token_start, or out-of-range fractions fail later with opaque errors."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/vector_ops.py",
      "lines": "16-32",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "pca_components_for_variance(threshold=0) returns one component even though zero components already explain zero required variance."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/steer_prefs.py",
      "lines": "45-49",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "The fallback for steered emotions can return fewer than four emotions despite the documented and tested 'at least four' expectation."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 220,
  "approve": false
}
